  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Previously, in VRChat, you could rotate and move objects with LT and joystick on the gamepad.\nHowever, this feature is not currently available only in desktop mode. Apparently, the LT / RT input of the gamepad seems to be disabled in desktop mode. This looks like a bug, because the tooltips that use LT / RT are displayed but you can't.\nOn the other hand, in VR mode, you can use LT / RT of the gamepad, and it is still possible to rotate and move objects with LT. (Although it is not necessary because there is a hand controller)\nIn desktop mode, the function was very convenient because you can not move the avatar's hand as in VR mode.\nSo I want VRChat to revive the input of LT / RT of the game pad in the desktop mode.",
